# Device patches and os-series replacements, one per line in application order.
#
# This file replaces os:patches/xnu/series, which lists three entries:
# zzz-boot-progress.patch and two XnuPrelink kit patches. patch_series entries
# are series files, and the boot-progress patch is not applied here, so only the
# two kit patches remain.
#
# zzz-boot-progress.patch (kept in this directory) adds boot_progress_stage()
# calls to arm_init.c, startup.c, bsd_init.c, kern_exec.c, kern_exit.c,
# video_console.c and pe_kprintf.c and includes <kern/boot_progress.h>. Neither
# the header nor an implementation exists in this UniXNU tree, and
# scripts/build-boot-progress.py (the builder the kernel script calls for
# CONFIG_XNU_BOOT_PROGRESS=1) is absent too. It also requires
# CONFIG_XNU_NATIVE_UFS=1, which GS101 cannot satisfy. Without the layer the
# kernel links with undefined _boot_progress_stage symbols, so the patch stays
# out of the series until a display-capable boot-progress layer exists.
#
# The device copy also drops one hunk that wraps sheng_pmgr_run() in
# boot_progress_stage() calls: that block only exists after a Qualcomm SoC's
# sheng-platform-power patch, which GS101 does not apply.
component:XnuPrelink/patches/xnu-10063.141.1-security-init.patch
